---
name: memory-reel-publish
description: >-
  Show the build summary, get the bot.ski rights sentence agreed word for word,
  pack the desk with the embedded packer, upload to bot.ski with no auth, handle
  every error code, and hand over the confirm link and review message.
---
# Memory Reel: publish

`D=/workspace/memory-reel/<handle>`. Needs `$D/bundle/`, `$D/cache/spec.json`, `$D/out/build-summary.json`.

## 1. Summary, then rights
Show, from `out/build-summary.json` (never recount by hand): eras, the `privacy_review` result (items listed, cut, left out by default, kept), `privacy_review.rule_cuts` (each include/exclude rule and how many posts it cut), months covered / not sampled, posts read and date range, beats, photos, clips, music videos, articles, privacy cuts (count + reasons from `out/privacy.md`), soundtrack mm:ss (L), and `zip_bytes` (pack first, then write the zip's size into `out/build-summary.json` as `zip_bytes`). Then quote `spec.rights.text` **word for word** and ask them to reply "I agree", then "upload". No paraphrase. Without both, stop and keep the bundle. The agreement covers this one upload only.

## 2. Pack
Always (re)write the packer below to `/workspace/memory-reel/tools/pack_bundle.py` verbatim before packing, even if a copy exists (stdlib only; templates don't carry files, so it lives in this skill).
`python3 /workspace/memory-reel/tools/pack_bundle.py $D <L> $D/out/reel-<yyyymmdd-hhmm>.zip`
Handle = desk folder name; spec = `$D/cache/spec.json`; bundle = `$D/bundle`. It checks paths against `spec.pathPattern`, file types by content, sizes, counts, one audio file, JSON depth/nodes/string length, links (only x.com, twitter.com, bot.ski; x.com/twitter.com links only to the person's own pages or `/i/status/` → else local `OTHERS_LINK`), `media/` references, og.jpg 1200×630, mp4 ≤ maxVideoSeconds (ffprobe if present), compression ratios, and runs the secret scan. It writes manifest.json (bytes + sha256). `manifest.template` is required: the spec's value if it names one, else `memory-reel` (server rule `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._@/-]{0,63}$`). The manifest is a strict object: only `format, handle, template, runtimeSec, files[{path, bytes, sha256}]`; the packer refuses anything else. A `SECRET` failure is local: show the hits; prose words like "token" and URLs are never flagged.

## 3. Upload (once, after "upload")
```
curl -sS -w "\n%{http_code}" -X POST "https://bot.ski/api/reels/upload?handle=<handle>" \
  -H "content-type: application/zip" -H "x-botski-rights-confirmed: yes" --data-binary @$D/out/reel-<…>.zip
```
If `privacy_review.status` isn't `answered` or `defaulted`, stop and finish the review first. No other headers, cookies or tokens. Save the response to `out/upload-<…>.json`; append date, zip, uploadId, status to `out/history.md`.

## 4. Errors (one fix per error; never loop)
| Code | Action |
|---|---|
| 202 | Go to 5. |
| E_ZIP, E_PATH, E_TYPE, E_HASH, E_MANIFEST, E_SCHEMA, E_MISSING, E_RATIO | My bug. Fix the named file (re-encode, fix JSON, rebuild manifest), repack, show what changed, upload once more. Same error twice → memory-reel-when-stuck. |
| E_LINK | A symlink or non-regular file in the zip (spec meaning). Replace it with a real file, repack, once. (Outside URLs in JSON come back as E_SCHEMA.) |
| E_SIZE, E_COUNT | Cut lowest-value media (dupes → low-like photos → clips), say what went, repack. |
| E_RIGHTS | Header missing: my bug. They already agreed; add it, resend once. |
| E_HANDLE | Handle can't host a reel. Tell them; stop. |
| E_NOT_OWNER | Handle belongs to another X account on bot.ski. Stop. |
| E_BUSY | Another upload is running. Ask, wait ~10 min, one retry. |
| E_RATE | Too many uploads (spec quota). Tell them when; no retry. |
| E_QUOTA, E_DISABLED | Server side. Keep the zip; try again only when they ask. |
| E_TAKEN_DOWN | Point to https://bot.ski/legal/copyright; stop. |
| other / 5xx | Say so once; keep the zip. |
Confirm-page codes they may report: E_AUTH (sign in as @handle), E_EXPIRED (re-upload the same zip for a new link, after asking and re-confirming rights), E_STATE (already done; check history.md).

## 5. Confirm link
> Uploaded, not public yet. Open this within 24 hours (by <expiresAt in their time zone>): <confirmUrl>
> Sign in with X as @<handle>, tick the rights box, press Confirm.
> Then: "<spec.review.message>"
> When it's approved: https://bot.ski/x/<handle>
Never open or confirm the link yourself. Once live, offer `memory-reel-record-video`.

## Packer (write verbatim to /workspace/memory-reel/tools/pack_bundle.py)
```python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Pack a Memory Reel desk into one botski-reel/1 zip. Stdlib only, no network, no credentials.
  python3 pack_bundle.py <desk> <runtimeSec> <out.zip>
<desk> = /workspace/memory-reel/<handle>; reads <desk>/cache/spec.json and <desk>/bundle/.
Fails with the spec's error code for anything the server would refuse; SECRET and OTHERS_LINK are local-only checks. @RichSilver · SKI-20261013-MEMORY-REEL"""
import hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, struct, subprocess, sys, zipfile

def fail(code, msg): sys.exit(f"pack_bundle: {code}: {msg}")

def img_size(b):
    if b[:8] == b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n": return struct.unpack(">II", b[16:24])
    if b[:2] != b"\xff\xd8": return None
    i = 2
    while i + 9 < len(b):
        if b[i] != 0xFF: i += 1; continue
        m = b[i + 1]
        if m in (0xD8, 0x01) or 0xD0 <= m <= 0xD7: i += 2; continue
        if 0xC0 <= m <= 0xCF and m not in (0xC4, 0xC8, 0xCC):
            h, w = struct.unpack(">HH", b[i + 5:i + 9]); return w, h
        i += 2 + struct.unpack(">H", b[i + 2:i + 4])[0]
    return None

MAGIC = {"jpg": lambda b: b[:3] == b"\xff\xd8\xff", "png": lambda b: b[:8] == b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n",
         "webp": lambda b: b[:4] == b"RIFF" and b[8:12] == b"WEBP", "mp4": lambda b: b[4:8] == b"ftyp",
         "mp3": lambda b: b[:3] == b"ID3" or (len(b) > 1 and b[0] == 0xFF and b[1] & 0xE0 == 0xE0)}
MAGIC["jpeg"] = MAGIC["jpg"]
SECRET = [("sk- key", r"\bsk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}"), ("Bearer", r"\bBearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9._~+/-]{16,}"),
          ("long hex", r"\b[0-9a-fA-F]{32,}\b"), ("long base64", r"(?<![A-Za-z0-9+/_-])(?=[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*[A-Z])(?=[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*[a-z])(?=[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*\d)[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]{40,}={0,2}"),
          ("email", r"\b[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*\.[A-Za-z]{2,}\b"),
          ("phone", r"(?<!\d)(?:\+\d{1,3}[\s.-]?)?\(?\d{3}\)?[\s.-]\d{3}[\s.-]\d{4}(?!\d)")]
MANIFEST_KEYS = {"format", "handle", "template", "runtimeSec", "files"}  # spec layout; the server rejects extras
OK_URL = re.compile(r"^https://(?:x\.com|twitter\.com|bot\.ski)/")

def walk(v, d, lim, rel, n):
    n[0] += 1
    if d > lim["maxJsonDepth"]: fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel} nests deeper than {lim['maxJsonDepth']}")
    if n[0] > lim["maxJsonNodes"]: fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel} has more than {lim['maxJsonNodes']} nodes")
    if isinstance(v, dict):
        for k, x in v.items(): walk(k, d + 1, lim, rel, n); walk(x, d + 1, lim, rel, n)
    elif isinstance(v, list):
        for x in v: walk(x, d + 1, lim, rel, n)
    elif isinstance(v, str):
        if len(v) > lim["maxJsonString"]: fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel} has a string over {lim['maxJsonString']} chars")
        if re.match(r"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*://", v) and not OK_URL.match(v):  # only real URLs; prose like "/imagine" or "note: x" is fine
            fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel}: link not allowed: {v[:80]}")
        if v.startswith("media/") and (".." in v or "//" in v):
            fail("E_PATH", f"{rel}: bad media reference {v[:80]}")

def main():
    if len(sys.argv) != 4: fail("USAGE", "pack_bundle.py <desk> <runtimeSec> <out.zip>")
    desk, out = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1]), sys.argv[3]
    handle, runtime = os.path.basename(desk).lower(), int(sys.argv[2])
    root, sp = os.path.join(desk, "bundle"), os.path.join(desk, "cache", "spec.json")
    if not os.path.exists(sp): fail("SPEC", f"missing {sp}: run curl -sS https://bot.ski/api/reels/spec -o {sp} (WebFetch only if curl fails)")
    spec = json.load(open(sp)); lim = spec["limits"]; rt = lim["runtimeSec"]
    path_re = re.compile(spec["pathPattern"])
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9_]{3,15}", handle): fail("E_HANDLE", handle)
    if not rt["min"] <= runtime <= rt["max"]: fail("E_SCHEMA", f"runtimeSec {runtime} outside {rt}")
    files = []
    for d, dirs, names in os.walk(root):
        for n in dirs + names:
            full = os.path.join(d, n); rel = os.path.relpath(full, root).replace(os.sep, "/")
            if os.path.islink(full): fail("E_LINK", f"{rel} is a symlink")
            if n in dirs: continue
            if not os.path.isfile(full): fail("E_LINK", f"{rel} is not a regular file")
            if rel == "manifest.json": continue
            if not path_re.match(rel): fail("E_PATH", rel)
            files.append(rel)
    for need in ("reel.json", "media/og.jpg"):
        if need not in files: fail("E_MISSING", need)
    audio = [f for f in files if f.endswith(".mp3")]
    if len(audio) > lim["maxAudioFiles"] or any(a != "media/track.mp3" for a in audio): fail("E_TYPE", f"audio: {audio}")
    if len(files) + 1 > lim["maxFiles"]: fail("E_COUNT", f"{len(files)+1} files")
    entries, total, hits = [], 0, []
    ffprobe = shutil.which("ffprobe")
    for rel in sorted(files):
        full = os.path.join(root, rel); b = open(full, "rb").read(); ext = rel.rsplit(".", 1)[1].lower()
        cap = lim["maxJsonBytes"] if ext == "json" else lim["maxFileBytes"]
        if len(b) > cap: fail("E_SIZE", f"{rel} is {len(b)} bytes (max {cap})")
        if ext == "json":
            try: doc = json.loads(b)
            except ValueError as e: fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel}: {e}")
            if not isinstance(doc, dict) or (rel == "reel.json" and "data" not in doc): fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel} needs {{data: ...}}")
            walk(doc, 0, lim, rel, [0]); text = b.decode()  # fresh node count per file
            if re.search(r"<\s*/?\s*(script|a|div|img|iframe|style|svg)\b", text, re.I): fail("E_SCHEMA", f"HTML in {rel}")
            urls = re.findall(r"https?://[^\s\"'\\]+", text)
            for u in urls:
                if not OK_URL.match(u): fail("E_SCHEMA", f"{rel} links outside x.com/twitter.com/bot.ski: {u}")
                m = re.match(r"https://(?:x|twitter)\.com/([A-Za-z0-9_]+)", u)
                if m and m.group(1).lower() not in (handle, "i", "hashtag", "search"): fail("OTHERS_LINK", f"{rel} links to someone else's X page: {u}")
            for ref in set(re.findall(r'"(media/[^"]+)"', text)):
                if ref not in files: fail("E_MISSING", f"{rel} points at {ref}")
            bare = re.sub(r"https?://[^\s\"'\\]+", " ", text)  # URLs are not secrets
            for name, pat in SECRET:
                for m in re.finditer(pat, bare): hits.append(f"{rel}: {name}: {m.group(0)[:60]}")
        else:
            if not MAGIC[ext](b): fail("E_TYPE", f"{rel} is not really .{ext}")
            if rel == "media/og.jpg" and img_size(b) != (1200, 630): fail("E_SCHEMA", f"og.jpg is {img_size(b)}, needs 1200x630")
            if ext == "mp4" and ffprobe:
                dur = float(subprocess.run([ffprobe, "-v", "error", "-show_entries", "format=duration", "-of", "csv=p=0", full],
                                           capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip() or 0)
                if dur > lim["maxVideoSeconds"]: fail("E_SIZE", f"{rel} runs {dur:.1f}s (max {lim['maxVideoSeconds']})")
        total += len(b)
        entries.append({"path": rel, "bytes": len(b), "sha256": hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()})
    if hits: fail("SECRET", "possible secrets/personal data, remove or confirm with a person:\n  " + "\n  ".join(hits))
    if total > lim["maxTotalBytes"]: fail("E_SIZE", f"total {total} bytes")
    template = spec.get("template") or "memory-reel"  # server: required, ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._@/-]{0,63}$
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._@/-]{0,63}", template): fail("E_MANIFEST", f"template {template!r}")
    manifest = {"format": spec["format"], "handle": handle, "template": template, "runtimeSec": runtime, "files": entries}
    if set(manifest) != MANIFEST_KEYS or any(set(e) != {"path", "bytes", "sha256"} for e in entries):
        fail("E_MANIFEST", f"manifest keys must be exactly {sorted(MANIFEST_KEYS)}")  # strict object
    with zipfile.ZipFile(out, "w") as z:
        z.writestr("manifest.json", json.dumps(manifest, indent=1), compress_type=zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED)
        for e in entries:
            z.write(os.path.join(root, e["path"]), e["path"],
                    compress_type=zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED if e["path"].endswith(".json") else zipfile.ZIP_STORED)
    with zipfile.ZipFile(out) as z:
        infos = z.infolist()
        if len(infos) > lim["maxEntries"]: fail("E_COUNT", f"{len(infos)} entries")
        for i in infos:
            r = i.file_size / max(i.compress_size, 1)
            if r > (lim["maxJsonRatio"] if i.filename.endswith(".json") else lim["maxMediaRatio"]):
                os.remove(out); fail("E_RATIO", f"{i.filename} compresses {r:.0f}:1")
    size = os.path.getsize(out)
    if size > lim["maxZipBytes"]: os.remove(out); fail("E_SIZE", f"zip {size} bytes")
    print(f"OK {out}: {size} bytes, {len(entries)+1} files, runtimeSec {runtime}, template {manifest.get('template', 'omitted')}")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```
